WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.726
(upbeat music)

00:00:01.726 --> 00:00:04.600
- I kinda felt like I
was prepared for a show.

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:06.360
I don't usually get
this fancy on the show.

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:07.193
- It's pretty rocking.

00:00:07.193 --> 00:00:08.190
- Thank you, I know, I like it.

00:00:08.190 --> 00:00:10.139
I feel like you would
wear especially this belt.

00:00:10.139 --> 00:00:10.972
(audience cheers)

00:00:10.972 --> 00:00:12.050
Yes, I like the belt.

00:00:12.050 --> 00:00:12.883
How are you doing?

00:00:12.883 --> 00:00:14.620
- I'm really excited to be here.

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:16.280
- I'm very nervous that you're here.

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:17.520
(Kelly giggles)
- You are?

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:18.353
You're so seasoned, though.

00:00:18.353 --> 00:00:20.920
- No, literally, like
you and Meryl are my...

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:22.150
That's my (Kelly sings).
- Oh, God.

00:00:22.150 --> 00:00:24.180
- Yeah, so they're like my favorite so-

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:25.180
- Look at these outfits.

00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:26.183
- I know we're very '80s.

00:00:26.183 --> 00:00:27.057
(audience applauding)

00:00:27.057 --> 00:00:28.590
- So great.

00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:30.945
- Okay, so congrats on the
Lifetime Achievement Award.

00:00:30.945 --> 00:00:32.680
- Thank you, thank you.
- That was this month.

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:34.245
- Yeah, the Grammy's.
- That's amazing.

00:00:34.245 --> 00:00:35.710
That's so cool's.

00:00:35.710 --> 00:00:37.350
It's getting that kind of stuff-

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:38.250
Is it weird for you-

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:39.520
Do get up there and like,

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:41.100
I mean, I can't even imagine being you

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:42.400
getting up there, winning
that kind of award

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:44.410
and thinking of all the amazing things

00:00:44.410 --> 00:00:45.930
that you've been a part
of, that you've done,

00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:47.034
that you've helped people.

00:00:47.034 --> 00:00:47.867
- Yeah, it's pretty amazing.

00:00:47.867 --> 00:00:49.300
And because we're going out on tour,

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:51.550
and I'm not hanging up my spurs yet.

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:52.383
- I know, I love that.
(crowd clapping)

00:00:52.383 --> 00:00:53.590
- It's really nice to get it now.

00:00:53.590 --> 00:00:54.530
- We're very excited

00:00:54.530 --> 00:00:55.805
- Was made the Staples.

00:00:55.805 --> 00:00:57.110
- I know.
- Right now.

00:00:57.110 --> 00:00:57.943
- My hero.

00:00:57.943 --> 00:00:59.270
- We literally were
texting about it last night

00:00:59.270 --> 00:01:00.140
and I was like, what?

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:00.973
I was gonna ask you

00:01:00.973 --> 00:01:03.060
who are some of you're
like heroes musically?

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:05.380
- Well, Mavis absolutely the Staple Singer

00:01:05.380 --> 00:01:07.080
from the time then they were backing up,

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:08.180
Dr. Martin Luther king.

00:01:08.180 --> 00:01:09.940
- Yeah.
(audience applauding)

00:01:09.940 --> 00:01:13.050
- And speaking of eighties how about,

00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:15.600
well, classic of all time Aretha Franklin.

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:16.830
- Oh my God, I love that.
- (audience applauding)

00:01:16.830 --> 00:01:18.100
- Ray Charles.

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:18.933
- Yeah

00:01:18.933 --> 00:01:20.790
- But Whitney for eighties, man.

00:01:20.790 --> 00:01:22.030
Whitney and you know-

00:01:22.030 --> 00:01:23.110
I mean, there's just so many

00:01:23.110 --> 00:01:26.600
and for roots artists like
me and Delbert McClinton

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:28.550
and Little Feat and people like that,

00:01:28.550 --> 00:01:29.750
it was a rough decade on them

00:01:29.750 --> 00:01:31.630
'cause they weren't playing
our kind of music on the radio

00:01:31.630 --> 00:01:33.330
until the end of the decade.

00:01:33.330 --> 00:01:35.840
And it was just by the
time Nick of Time won

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:36.673
people went, "Wow."

00:01:36.673 --> 00:01:39.330
That's just all kinds
of music mixed into one.

00:01:39.330 --> 00:01:41.200
- And that's why you're
one of my favorites.

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:42.267
Like I-
- Thank you.

00:01:42.267 --> 00:01:43.250
- And that's Linda Ronstadt
that's one of my favorite.

00:01:43.250 --> 00:01:45.710
I just love any artist that's like-

00:01:45.710 --> 00:01:47.020
Doesn't pigeonhole themselves

00:01:47.020 --> 00:01:48.820
because that's my
favorite thing about music

00:01:48.820 --> 00:01:51.410
is I love country music and
I love pop, I love so...

00:01:51.410 --> 00:01:52.843
I grew up on Nirvana, I
grew up on everything.

00:01:52.843 --> 00:01:54.320
- I know, I love it too.

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:55.610
That's one of the reasons I love you

00:01:55.610 --> 00:01:56.842
because you're really-
- Oh, thank you.

00:01:56.842 --> 00:01:57.800
(audience applauding)

00:01:57.800 --> 00:02:00.030
- Thank God, I get it from you.

00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:00.863
I love that-

00:02:00.863 --> 00:02:02.300
- But I love (mumbles).

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:03.470
- Oh my God, me too, me too.

00:02:03.470 --> 00:02:04.620
I'm just talking with Bonnie Raitt.

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:06.147
Don't worry about America.

00:02:06.147 --> 00:02:09.120
We're back with Bonnie Raitt,
this celebration of the 1980s

00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:11.180
because it's my birthday week.

00:02:11.180 --> 00:02:14.570
So you, I heard that you
briefly worked with Prince

00:02:14.570 --> 00:02:15.499
in the '80s.

00:02:15.499 --> 00:02:16.332
Is that correct?
- I did.

00:02:16.332 --> 00:02:17.357
I did Prince called me up and said,

00:02:17.357 --> 00:02:18.837
"Hey, you weren't treated right.

00:02:18.837 --> 00:02:20.147
"Come on over to Paisley Park.

00:02:20.147 --> 00:02:21.230
"Let's make a record together."

00:02:21.230 --> 00:02:22.607
- I love that.
(audience applauding)

00:02:22.607 --> 00:02:25.760
- And I said, if we
can meet in the middle,

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:27.280
I don't necessarily wanna
do a whole Prince thing

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:28.810
and you don't wanna do
a Bonnie Raitt thing.

00:02:28.810 --> 00:02:29.643
So-
- Yeah.

00:02:29.643 --> 00:02:32.790
I had a ski accident and fell on my thumb

00:02:32.790 --> 00:02:34.530
and had to be in a cast for two months.

00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:36.710
So I had to postpone working with him.

00:02:36.710 --> 00:02:37.549
- This is why I don't work out.

00:02:37.549 --> 00:02:38.382
(all laughing)

00:02:38.382 --> 00:02:41.390
- And then I was like,
35, 40 pounds heavier.

00:02:41.390 --> 00:02:43.327
And I went, "If I do
a video with this guy,

00:02:43.327 --> 00:02:45.777
"if song works and it's really sexy,

00:02:45.777 --> 00:02:47.010
"I gotta do something."

00:02:47.010 --> 00:02:48.970
I said, "I gotta work on this."

00:02:48.970 --> 00:02:52.210
So I used the cast as an
excuse to lose weight.

00:02:52.210 --> 00:02:54.610
And I just, I said, I
better quit drinking too,

00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:55.793
because it gets in your 30s

00:02:55.793 --> 00:02:57.790
that you put on pounds a lot easier.

00:02:57.790 --> 00:02:58.882
- I I've noticed.

00:02:58.882 --> 00:03:00.355
(all laughing)

00:03:00.355 --> 00:03:03.000
- So I ended up hanging out
with some friends of mine

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:04.787
that were sober and I
went, "You know what?

00:03:04.787 --> 00:03:06.370
"This feels really good."

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:08.455
So I lost 20 pounds before
I worked with Prince.

00:03:08.455 --> 00:03:09.288
(audience applauding)

00:03:09.288 --> 00:03:10.121
- I love it.

00:03:10.121 --> 00:03:10.954
That's what did it.

00:03:10.954 --> 00:03:11.820
- And that's kinda what did it

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:14.100
'cause I was so terrified
of being in a video

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:16.840
with him and not like looking

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:18.687
and saying all that sexy
stuff to me and going,

00:03:18.687 --> 00:03:20.698
"I don't think this people
are gonna believe that."

00:03:20.698 --> 00:03:21.531
(audience laughing)

00:03:21.531 --> 00:03:23.130
- I have to ask this because I didn't know

00:03:23.130 --> 00:03:25.120
that you had like a bagpipe phase.

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:27.730
- Oh my God, our family is Scott.

00:03:27.730 --> 00:03:29.690
Our family is Scottish roots.

00:03:29.690 --> 00:03:31.540
- Okay, but a lot of
people have Scottish roots

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:33.110
that don't play the bagpipe (laughs).

00:03:33.110 --> 00:03:35.450
- But I really love the sound of bagpipes.

00:03:35.450 --> 00:03:36.300
- It's beautiful.

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:40.180
- I got on a consignment.

00:03:40.180 --> 00:03:41.013
- Yeah.

00:03:41.013 --> 00:03:41.940
- Thrifts, whatever you call that?

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:42.773
- Yeah.
- The sh...

00:03:42.773 --> 00:03:44.523
When you get used stuff, the newspaper.

00:03:45.460 --> 00:03:46.293
You remember those?

00:03:46.293 --> 00:03:47.264
(all laughing)
- I do.

00:03:47.264 --> 00:03:48.660
- And it was for sale and I bought 'em.

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:49.493
- Yeah.

00:03:49.493 --> 00:03:51.600
- And I asked I in my college paper,

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:53.770
I advertised in the want ads for anybody

00:03:53.770 --> 00:03:55.060
that knew how to blow.

00:03:55.060 --> 00:03:57.643
- Yeah.
(all laughing)

00:03:59.740 --> 00:04:01.984
- And then it said like
this "Bagpipes" underneath

00:04:01.984 --> 00:04:03.440
and that was my ad.

00:04:03.440 --> 00:04:04.273
- Oh my God, I was like,

00:04:04.273 --> 00:04:06.010
"What kind of results happened after?"

00:04:06.010 --> 00:04:08.760
- And then I got, I said
"know how to blow bagpipes,

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:10.600
Freshman wants to learn".

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:12.403
But my-
- Freshman wants to learn.

00:04:13.530 --> 00:04:17.820
- And my housemates at my dorm
they wouldn't let me learn.

00:04:17.820 --> 00:04:20.050
'cause it just sounds like
someone's being strangled.

00:04:20.050 --> 00:04:20.883
- It's was so loud.

00:04:20.883 --> 00:04:21.716
- Yeah, oh it's terrible.

00:04:21.716 --> 00:04:22.549
- Yeah.

00:04:22.549 --> 00:04:23.470
- Really bad.
- But it is beautiful.

00:04:23.470 --> 00:04:25.030
- And I was like passing out from,

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:26.700
I didn't have the air to
blow through that thing.

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:27.670
- To sustain, yeah.
- Yeah.

00:04:27.670 --> 00:04:28.740
- Yeah, it seems hard.

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:29.900
- I like it but too hard.

00:04:29.900 --> 00:04:31.180
I know it was too hard for me,

00:04:31.180 --> 00:04:32.430
I'm glad I stuck with the guitar.

00:04:32.430 --> 00:04:33.620
- I think we all are.

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:34.664
Yeah.
- Thank you (laughs).

00:04:34.664 --> 00:04:35.497
(audience applauding)

00:04:35.497 --> 00:04:36.510
- I think I was a solid decision.

00:04:36.510 --> 00:04:38.430
So wait, is this 21?

00:04:38.430 --> 00:04:39.570
This album, is it number 21?

00:04:39.570 --> 00:04:40.650
- Yes, number 21.

00:04:40.650 --> 00:04:41.483
That's amazing.

00:04:41.483 --> 00:04:42.525
(audience applauding)

00:04:42.525 --> 00:04:44.890
So what out of all the albums

00:04:44.890 --> 00:04:47.590
what do you feel like
makes this one different?

00:04:47.590 --> 00:04:48.760
- Well, I wanted to write,

00:04:48.760 --> 00:04:50.282
I was really inspired by, especially

00:04:50.282 --> 00:04:53.310
because we lost John Prine
this last year to COVID

00:04:53.310 --> 00:04:56.920
and I love his story songs
like, "Angel from Montgomery"

00:04:56.920 --> 00:05:00.090
and Donald and Lydia and
Jackson Browne's early records.

00:05:00.090 --> 00:05:02.140
I love that simplicity

00:05:02.140 --> 00:05:04.940
of a finger picking song telling a story.

00:05:04.940 --> 00:05:07.560
So this record has a
couple of mine on there

00:05:07.560 --> 00:05:11.720
that are a third person
kind of story taking

00:05:11.720 --> 00:05:13.660
on the character of
somebody else besides me.

00:05:13.660 --> 00:05:14.493
- Yeah.

00:05:14.493 --> 00:05:15.326
- 'Cause I really find-

00:05:15.326 --> 00:05:16.159
- Which is fun 'cause you can go-

00:05:16.159 --> 00:05:17.552
- Mind all my personal life already and I-

00:05:17.552 --> 00:05:18.883
(Kelly laughs)

00:05:18.883 --> 00:05:19.716
- In the first 20.

00:05:19.716 --> 00:05:20.790
- Yeah, exactly.
- Yeah.

00:05:20.790 --> 00:05:21.980
- So that's different from me.

00:05:21.980 --> 00:05:23.060
I went back to my roots

00:05:23.060 --> 00:05:25.870
kinda just played folk guitar
and sang these story songs.

00:05:25.870 --> 00:05:27.750
And then I wrote a rocker that's,

00:05:27.750 --> 00:05:29.570
to my guitar player's track

00:05:29.570 --> 00:05:31.160
that was just too good to give up.

00:05:31.160 --> 00:05:33.340
I had to play dual guitar with him

00:05:33.340 --> 00:05:36.270
and I wrote a song for
what all the people we lost

00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:37.950
even for the ones who didn't make it.

00:05:37.950 --> 00:05:40.420
- Yeah, so wait, what's the
story behind the title track,

00:05:40.420 --> 00:05:41.290
"Just Like That".

00:05:41.290 --> 00:05:43.610
- "Just Like That", I was
watching the evening news

00:05:43.610 --> 00:05:46.350
and sometimes they have a
human interest story at the end

00:05:46.350 --> 00:05:48.787
and they said, "Oh, we're
gonna follow this woman

00:05:48.787 --> 00:05:50.587
"to the house of the man

00:05:50.587 --> 00:05:52.801
"who received her son's donated heart."

00:05:52.801 --> 00:05:53.830
- Oh wow.

00:05:53.830 --> 00:05:55.650
- And they followed her into the house

00:05:55.650 --> 00:05:56.980
and he said, just sit down.

00:05:56.980 --> 00:06:00.007
He said, "Would you like to
put your head on my chest

00:06:00.007 --> 00:06:01.410
"and listen to your son's heart?"

00:06:01.410 --> 00:06:03.420
And I lost it.

00:06:03.420 --> 00:06:04.253
I just lost it.

00:06:04.253 --> 00:06:06.540
And I was so moved by the story

00:06:06.540 --> 00:06:08.350
that I ended up writing a character

00:06:08.350 --> 00:06:09.940
and writing a song about what it would be

00:06:09.940 --> 00:06:11.550
like for both those people.

00:06:11.550 --> 00:06:12.481
- Yeah.
- To experience that.

00:06:12.481 --> 00:06:13.550
(audience applauding)

00:06:13.550 --> 00:06:14.960
- Oh my God, what a line?

00:06:14.960 --> 00:06:16.148
- Yeah, oh my God.

00:06:16.148 --> 00:06:17.606
(audience applauding)

00:06:17.606 --> 00:06:20.740
- That's so incredibly sad,
but beautiful at the same time.

00:06:20.740 --> 00:06:21.573
- And that's how I feel about it.

00:06:21.573 --> 00:06:22.730
- Yeah.
- I mean,

00:06:22.730 --> 00:06:24.930
we need stories that
really open your heart

00:06:24.930 --> 00:06:26.520
in these difficult times.

00:06:26.520 --> 00:06:27.760
- Yeah.

00:06:27.760 --> 00:06:30.390
I can't let you leave
this room without talk...

00:06:30.390 --> 00:06:32.810
I know I've mentioned it
to you before but your,

00:06:32.810 --> 00:06:36.040
I can't express to you
what happened inside of me

00:06:36.040 --> 00:06:36.873
when I heard...

00:06:36.873 --> 00:06:39.260
I love "Love Me Like a Man"
on the regular version.

00:06:39.260 --> 00:06:43.900
But the live version
specifically, like on your thing,

00:06:43.900 --> 00:06:45.057
it'll be like "What your favorites are,

00:06:45.057 --> 00:06:46.140
"what you've listened to most?"

00:06:46.140 --> 00:06:48.475
And you're like, "That is
literally my favorite."

00:06:48.475 --> 00:06:49.308
It's that one.
- Thank you.

00:06:49.308 --> 00:06:50.970
And "I Never Loved a
Man" by Aretha Franklin.

00:06:50.970 --> 00:06:52.017
Those are my two I listen to the most,

00:06:52.017 --> 00:06:53.980
- I love that's my
favorite song of hers too.

00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:54.813
- That's my favorite song.

00:06:54.813 --> 00:06:57.040
- My other, if I could only have one song,

00:06:57.040 --> 00:06:57.873
that would be the one.

00:06:57.873 --> 00:06:59.010
- That's my favorite

00:06:59.010 --> 00:06:59.843
- Oh, my God, that's I love...

00:06:59.843 --> 00:07:01.006
Oh, I know that's why we relate-

00:07:01.006 --> 00:07:01.839
- Those are my two.

00:07:01.839 --> 00:07:02.672
- We're like sisters.
- I'm telling you, I'm fine.

00:07:02.672 --> 00:07:04.700
- But I love that live version.

00:07:04.700 --> 00:07:06.410
Thank you so much.

00:07:06.410 --> 00:07:10.940
- It is literally just so amazing
and so soulful and so raw.

00:07:10.940 --> 00:07:12.477
It's just so good.

00:07:12.477 --> 00:07:13.528
- Thank you.

00:07:13.528 --> 00:07:14.430
- And honestly too,

00:07:14.430 --> 00:07:16.810
I'm gonna say this is no shade to anyone,

00:07:16.810 --> 00:07:19.210
but it's also you're from a time too.

00:07:19.210 --> 00:07:23.010
Like people had to be
able to be amazing live.

00:07:23.010 --> 00:07:23.843
You know what I'm saying?

00:07:23.843 --> 00:07:24.900
Like.
- Yeah.

00:07:24.900 --> 00:07:25.733
(audience applauding)

00:07:25.733 --> 00:07:26.566
You, it wasn't a time

00:07:26.566 --> 00:07:28.120
when you could digitally fix everything.

00:07:28.120 --> 00:07:31.610
It wasn't and that carries over
and it's just such a lesson.

00:07:31.610 --> 00:07:34.057
Like I was just talking to my
stylist, like "You performed

00:07:34.057 --> 00:07:35.800
"I don't figure what would
show it was we were watching."

00:07:35.800 --> 00:07:38.380
And you got on stage
and it was like, "Well."

00:07:38.380 --> 00:07:40.750
And that's how you were
supposed to do it everyone.

00:07:40.750 --> 00:07:41.583
- Oh, sweet.

00:07:41.583 --> 00:07:43.100
- Like it was like, it literally is.

00:07:43.100 --> 00:07:45.970
It's like, you just,
you sound amazing live

00:07:45.970 --> 00:07:47.270
and that's not true for everyone,

00:07:47.270 --> 00:07:48.103
not throwing shade at anyone.

00:07:48.103 --> 00:07:50.230
I'm just saying that's what it is and-

00:07:50.230 --> 00:07:52.380
- Well, I didn't sell a lot
of records the first 20 years

00:07:52.380 --> 00:07:54.540
and then even with "Nick of
Time" was like a little blip

00:07:54.540 --> 00:07:56.000
of a couple of albums that did well.

00:07:56.000 --> 00:07:58.540
But I knew if I just did
every show really good

00:07:58.540 --> 00:08:00.251
that people would keep coming to see me.

00:08:00.251 --> 00:08:01.084
- You know what?

00:08:01.084 --> 00:08:01.917
That's so true.

00:08:01.917 --> 00:08:04.050
Everybody's always worried
about winning awards.

00:08:04.050 --> 00:08:05.100
And my thing is like,

00:08:05.100 --> 00:08:06.620
I don't really care
about winning the award.

00:08:06.620 --> 00:08:08.010
I just want the performance slot

00:08:08.010 --> 00:08:10.540
because I just wanna prove
exactly what I can do.

00:08:10.540 --> 00:08:11.373
That's it.

00:08:11.373 --> 00:08:12.380
- I'm totally with you because I mean

00:08:12.380 --> 00:08:14.340
give me a live show and
I'll prove what I'm.

00:08:14.340 --> 00:08:15.240
- Yeah, that's what...

00:08:15.240 --> 00:08:16.920
Yeah, there's something
that happens in us.

00:08:16.920 --> 00:08:17.872
I love that.

00:08:17.872 --> 00:08:19.600
- So thank you for
appreciating that live version

00:08:19.600 --> 00:08:20.433
because it's-

00:08:20.433 --> 00:08:21.596
- It's amazing.

00:08:21.596 --> 00:08:22.429
- Thank you.

00:08:22.429 --> 00:08:23.760
- And that just doesn't exist.

00:08:23.760 --> 00:08:26.020
I don't feel anymore with artists, so...

00:08:26.020 --> 00:08:27.680
but wait, are you looking forward
to getting back out there?

00:08:27.680 --> 00:08:28.970
'Cause I know a lot of artists are,

00:08:28.970 --> 00:08:29.863
cause everybody's been on
hold for like two years.

00:08:29.863 --> 00:08:32.400
- Two and a half years
since we had a live.

00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:34.250
Last week was the first warmup shows.

00:08:34.250 --> 00:08:36.026
First audience I heard
in two and a half years.

00:08:36.026 --> 00:08:36.886
- Does it feel good.

00:08:36.886 --> 00:08:37.800
- Oh my God, I was like-

00:08:37.800 --> 00:08:39.730
- Yeah, you feed off of it.

00:08:39.730 --> 00:08:40.990
- I mean, it was the first time

00:08:40.990 --> 00:08:42.240
I'd sung "Angel from Montgomery"

00:08:42.240 --> 00:08:43.570
since John passed and-

00:08:43.570 --> 00:08:44.403
- Oh wow.

00:08:44.403 --> 00:08:46.130
"I Can't Make You Love
Me" was like transcendent

00:08:46.130 --> 00:08:48.010
and I've got a couple
of new guys in the band

00:08:48.010 --> 00:08:49.510
and I hadn't seen my guys

00:08:49.510 --> 00:08:52.260
until we got in the studio
last June to make my album.

00:08:52.260 --> 00:08:54.760
That was a long after 50 years on the road

00:08:54.760 --> 00:08:55.940
to have that much time

00:08:55.940 --> 00:08:57.590
without playing in front of people.

00:08:57.590 --> 00:08:59.390
- 'Cause I also think people don't realize

00:08:59.390 --> 00:09:01.120
like your band is like your second family.

00:09:01.120 --> 00:09:03.593
You see them sometimes more
than your actual family.

00:09:03.593 --> 00:09:04.426
- Yeah.

00:09:04.426 --> 00:09:06.980
- So that's a really big hole of isolation

00:09:06.980 --> 00:09:08.720
like especially for a creative person.

00:09:08.720 --> 00:09:10.370
- Well, it's a good thing we have texting

00:09:10.370 --> 00:09:11.570
and sending-
- FaceTime-

00:09:11.570 --> 00:09:12.700
- Dog pictures and everything.

00:09:12.700 --> 00:09:13.533
- Yeah.

00:09:13.533 --> 00:09:15.740
Anyway, Bonnie is for
forming later in the show,

00:09:15.740 --> 00:09:16.835
so stick around.

00:09:16.835 --> 00:09:18.954
Her new album is called, "Just Like That"

00:09:18.954 --> 00:09:20.270
and it's out tomorrow.

00:09:20.270 --> 00:09:22.510
You can also go online to
find tickets for her tour

00:09:22.510 --> 00:09:23.790
which is happening right now.

00:09:23.790 --> 00:09:25.310
You gotta go check her out,

00:09:25.310 --> 00:09:27.860
'cause not many artists
sell like this live people.

